From 1517326fcc9dfdb9acb24f42472366ac1b4b8237 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean Young <sean@mess.org>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 13:13:29 +0100
Subject: media: meson-ir-tx: Ensure clock is disabled on unbind
Git-commit: 1517326fcc9dfdb9acb24f42472366ac1b4b8237
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes

clk_prepare_enable() needs a call to clk_disable_unprepare() on
driver unbind. Make it devm managed.

Fixes: 49be1c78d575 ("media: rc: introduce Meson IR TX driver")
Signed-off-by: Sean Young <sean@mess.org>
Reviewed-by: Martin Blumenstingl <martin.blumenstingl@googlemail.com>
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Reviewed-by: Hans Verkuil <hverkuil+cisco@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 drivers/media/rc/meson-ir-tx.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/rc/meson-ir-tx.c b/drivers/media/rc/meson-ir-tx.c
index fded2c256f2a..6beb9e97453d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/rc/meson-ir-tx.c
+++ b/drivers/media/rc/meson-ir-tx.c
@@ -288,11 +288,12 @@ static int meson_irtx_mod_clock_probe(struct meson_irtx *ir,
 	if (!np)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
-	clock = devm_clk_get(ir->dev, "xtal");
-	if (IS_ERR(clock) || clk_prepare_enable(clock))
+	*clk_nr = IRB_MOD_XTAL3_CLK;
+
+	clock = devm_clk_get_enabled(ir->dev, "xtal");
+	if (IS_ERR(clock))
 		return -ENODEV;
 
-	*clk_nr = IRB_MOD_XTAL3_CLK;
 	ir->clk_rate = clk_get_rate(clock) / 3;
 
 	if (ir->clk_rate < IRB_MOD_1US_CLK_RATE) {
-- 
